You are given a string $S$, consisting only of lowercase English letters. Each letter has a numeric value where:$a = 1, b = 2, \dots, 
z = 26$.Your task is to compute the cumulative alphabetic gap sum of the string with the following rules:Consider each adjacent pair of
characters in $S \rightarrow (S[i], S[i+1])$.Compute the gap between them as:$$\text{gap} = \text{value}(S[i+1]) - \text{value}(S[i])$$Add 
each computed gap to a cumulative sum.Do not consider the pair $(\text{last character}, \text{first character})$ (i.e., not circular).
Return the final cumulative sum.Input FormatA single string $S$ ($1 \le \vert{}S\vert{} \le 10^5$).



  
#include <iostream>
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
   string s;
   cin>>s;    
   int sum=0;
   for(int i=1;i<s.size();i++){
       int gap=(s[i]-'a'+1)-(s[i-1]-'a'+1);
       sum+=gap;
   }
   cout<<sum<<endl;
    return 0;
}
